{"level":"info","message":"## 1. Reflect on Your Situation\n\nAs a software developer, being unemployed at 35 can be unsettling. It's essential to acknowledge this feeling and consider it an opportunity for growth.\n\n**State your assumptions explicitly**: You are concerned about your job security as a software developer.\n\n**Present multiple interpretations**: Being unemployed can lead to feelings of inadequacy or frustration. However, you can also use this time to explore new opportunities, update your skills, and network with professionals in the field.\n\n## 2. Identify Areas for Improvement\n\nConsider the following:\n\n* Update your online presence (e.g., LinkedIn profile, personal website) to showcase your skills and experience.\n* Invest in relevant courses or training programs to enhance your technical expertise.\n* Network with other developers to stay informed about industry trends and job opportunities.\n\n**Ask yourself**: \"Would a senior engineer say this is an overcomplicated situation?\" If yes, simplify your approach by focusing on essential tasks.\n\n## 3. Create a Plan for Job Search\n\nDevelop a plan to increase your visibility in the job market:\n\n* Update your resume and cover letter to highlight relevant experience and skills.\n* Utilize job search platforms (e.g., LinkedIn, Glassdoor) to find suitable positions.\n* Reach out to professional contacts for referrals or advice.\n\n**Match existing style**: Tailor your approach to align with industry standards and best practices. Consider seeking guidance from a mentor or career coach if needed.\n\n## 4. Execute the Plan\n\nImplement your plan by:\n\n1. Updating online presence: [Verify update]\n2. Investing in training: [Verify completion]\n3. Networking: [Verify connections]\n\n**Define success criteria**: Measure progress through job search metrics (e.g., number of applications, interviews). Adjust your approach as needed to achieve desired outcomes.\n\n**Strong success criteria**: Focus on specific, measurable goals (e.g., \"Secure an interview within the next two weeks\"). This will enable you to track your progress and make adjustments accordingly."}
