{"level":"info","message":"## Feeling Unemployed as a Software Developer\n\n**Accept uncertainty, and clarify assumptions.**\n\nDon't assume being unemployed at 35 is unusual or reflects on your abilities.\n\n**Simplicity First**\n\nDon't overthink it. Focus on the facts:\n\n* You're capable of finding another job.\n* Many developers face similar situations.\n\n## Surgical Changes\n\n**Touch only what you must. Clean up only your own mess.**\n\nYou don't need to \"fix\" or \"improve\" anything about yourself.\n\n**Goal-Driven Execution**\n\n**Define success criteria. Loop until verified.**\n\nSuccess: You've found a new job or are taking steps to find one.\n\nLoop:\n1. **Explore career options**: Research and update your resume.\n2. **Network and build connections**: Attend events, join online communities, and reach out to colleagues.\n3. **Apply for jobs**: Tailor applications and submit them efficiently.\n4. **Prepare for interviews**: Review common questions and practice responses.\n\nKeep track of progress and adjust the plan as needed.\n\n## Continuous Improvement\n\nReview your approach regularly and consider feedback from others.\n\nIf you need help or have questions, don't hesitate to ask.\n\nBest of luck in your job search!"}
