{"level":"info","message":"**Anxiety and uncertainty are normal, but don't let them define you.**\n\nAs a software developer at 35, being unemployed can be challenging, but it's not uncommon for people in the industry to change roles or industries multiple times throughout their career.\n\n**Focus on your strengths and skills.** You've invested time and effort into developing your technical expertise. Highlight these skills and how they can benefit potential employers.\n\n**Expand your network.** Attend conferences, join online communities, and connect with professionals in your field to stay updated on industry trends and job opportunities.\n\n**Create a personal project or contribute to open-source projects.** Showcase your skills by building something meaningful or helping others through collaborative coding efforts.\n\n**Stay adaptable and proactive.** Continuously learn new technologies and be prepared to pivot if needed.\n\nRemember, being unemployed at 35 as a software developer is not a reflection of your worth or abilities. It's an opportunity to recharge, refocus, and explore new possibilities.\n\n **Keep moving forward.**"}
