{"level":"info","message":"## Step 1: Understand the Situation\nYou are 35 and unemployed, which can be a challenging situation for anyone. However, as a software developer, you have a valuable skill set that can be applied to various industries.\n\n## Step 2: Identify Key Factors\nConsider your age, experience, and skills as a software developer. Think about how these factors can help you find employment or start a new project.\n\n## Step 3: Focus on Opportunities\nInstead of dwelling on the negative aspects of being unemployed, focus on the opportunities that come with this situation. You have time to:\n- Update your skills and knowledge\n- Network with other professionals in the industry\n- Explore different areas of software development that interest you\n\n## Step 4: Create a Plan\nDevelop a plan to find employment or start a new project. This could include:\n- Updating your resume and online profiles\n- Attending job fairs and networking events\n- Creating a portfolio of your work or projects\n- Exploring freelance opportunities or starting a side business\n\n## Step 5: Stay Positive and Motivated\nRemind yourself that being unemployed at 35 is not the end. Many people have successfully transitioned to new careers or started their own businesses in this age group.\n\nThe final answer is: **You should focus on the opportunities that come with being unemployed, update your skills and knowledge, and create a plan to find employment or start a new project.**"}
